?><article class="glass panel prose"><h1><?=h(t('privacy'))?></h1><p><strong>What you agree to:</strong> Your uploaded photos and your display name may be shown on a publicly visible TV or computer screen after an administrator approves them. Anyone who can see that screen can see your photos.</p><h2>Data collected</h2><p>We store your chosen name, a hash of your visitor credential and recovery code, images, consent timestamp, consent text version and a keyed hash of your IP address. We do not keep your original image filenames or raw IP addresses.</p><h2>Photos and metadata</h2><p>We validate, resize and re-encode accepted image files to strip EXIF metadata such as GPS location. Photos are stored in a restricted upload folder. JPG, PNG and WEBP only, up to 5 MB each, five per request and twenty per visitor.</p><h2>Control and retention</h2><p>Pending photos never appear publicly. You can delete any photo or withdraw consent using My Photos. Withdrawing deletes all photo files and removes them from the slideshow. The default photo retention is 90 days once the cleanup task is configured. Copies photographed or cached by third parties cannot be recalled.</p><h2>Local deployment</h2><p>This assignment is intended for a local WampServer deployment. For public hosting, HTTPS, a stronger recovery mechanism, server hardening and privacy-law review are essential.</p></article><?php page_end(); ?>
